From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marcus Ramberg <marcus@means.no>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:53:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/20] firmware: qcom: scm: allow QSEECOM on the Fairphone 5

The Fairphone 5 (QCM6490) runs a QSEE that carries the fingerprint
trusted application, so the machine needs to be on the QSEECOM
allowlist for the TEE driver to bind.

Signed-off-by: Marcus Ramberg <marcus@means.no>
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index c4c30fc983d6..80873a2660d3 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2678,6 +2678,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "dell,latitude-7455" },
 	{ .compatible = "dell,xps13-9345" },
 	{ .compatible = "ecs,liva-qc710" },
+	{ .compatible = "fairphone,fp5" },
 	{ .compatible = "honor,magicbook-art-14-snapdragon" },
 	{ .compatible = "hp,elitebook-ultra-g1q" },
 	{ .compatible = "hp,omnibook-x14" },
